{
  "//": "GRAVITY BEACON - each tap drops a gravity well that pulls for about a second. You shape the trajectory; you never push the ball directly.",
  "//physics": "Falloff is inverse-LINEAR, not inverse-square: bimp * (tapX - bx) has magnitude G / max(d, 40). Inverse-square spans a 14x force range across this playfield and the ball slingshots off the near end of it. bsc caps the speed at 5 px/frame.",
  "//engine": "Expressions cap at 32 RPN tokens. ifElse(falseValue, trueValue, condition) reads its condition LAST. Every equation reads the previous frame's values, so intermediates land one frame late.",
  "header": {
    "apiLevel": 7,
    "width": 400,
    "height": 400,
    "profiles": 513,
    "contentDescription": "Gravity Beacon: tap to place a gravity well and curve the ball into the goal"
  },
  "root": {
    "canvas": {
      "modifiers": [
        "fillMaxSize"
      ],
      "commands": [
